    "notes": "RESTORED after an accidental full-schema overwrite via the Ruleset/Blending modal (compileVisualToJDM regenerates the whole schema from its own axes/profileConfig state and does not know how to represent these custom decisionTableNodes -- opening and saving that modal WILL wipe this again until it gets a proper 'custom rule' mode).\n\nConfirmed via Report.pdf's source legend: S/R (Sensitive knob) is sourced Kuisioner ONLY (Q2), no API icon at all -- pure axis_codes threshold on the merged 'sensitivity' dimension, no vision fusion, matching classic Baumann methodology (D/O and S/R are self-report in the original BSTI; P/N and W/T are Wardah's own photo-verified extension beyond stock Baumann). P/N (Pigmented knob) is Kuisioner + API 'sbg penguat' (booster) -- kuisioner-dominant (0.8 form / 0.2 vision), not 50/50. D/O (sebum) is form-only (caller must never send vision_signals.sebum). W/T (aging) is vision+DOB-only, both wrinkle AND age must be healthy for Tight (caller must never send a form dimension named wrinkle/age_over_30, only vision_signals.wrinkle and vision_signals.age_over_30).\n\nQ2's has_acne/has_stinger condition_map flags are captured on the form (skinverse_q1_q6) but deliberately not split into scored dimensions right now -- current scope is just the 4-letter blending code. q2_acne/q2_stinger are already registered in reference-service for when Product Mapping's Sub Sensitive column or Report.pdf's two separate skin-signal knobs get built.\n\nP/N (Pigmentation) weight is LOCKED at 0.8 form / 0.2 vision — form must stay > 50%. Per the guideline, a photo darkspot reading must never be allowed to flip the P/N letter on its own; the questionnaire answer stays dominant. If this gets tweaked live during a demo (e.g. to show the Blending tab changing a score), REVERT the pigmentation dimension_fusion back to {form: 0.8, vision: 0.2} afterward — do not leave a different ratio in place permanently.",
    "axis_codes": {
